(a) Any animal may be impounded if:
(1) It is not under restraint or is at large;
(2) It is livestock and is not being maintained in accordance with this chapter;
(3) It is a hazardous animal that, on or after January 1, 2010, the owner has not registered as required by an animal control officer or the hazardous animal is not being confined as required pursuant to this chapter;
(4) It is a guard animal and is not kept in accordance with the provisions of this chapter;
(5) It does not have a visible collar with a valid and current rabies vaccination tag affixed as required by this chapter;
(6) It has been abandoned as prohibited by this chapter;
(7) It has bitten or is reasonably suspected of biting another animal or human and is being held for the required quarantine period under the rules of the board of health; or
(8) It has been abused as prohibited by this chapter.
(b) Said animal shall be impounded according to such rules and regulations now or hereafter prescribed by law or by the resolutions and ordinances of the governing authority for the detention, control and disposition of animals. All impounded animals shall be housed and cared for at the Hall County Animal Shelter or such other facility as may be required to securely confine the animal if the animal cannot be maintained at the Hall County Animal Shelter.
(c) Any animal impounded after a finding by an animal control officer that it has been abused pursuant to this chapter shall not be released to the owner unless the owner demonstrates to animal control that the animal will not be subjected to the same or different conditions upon its release that originally led to or will lead to a violation of this chapter within seven days of an animal control officer's impoundment of the animal.
(d) Any animal whose owner fails to comply with paragraph (c) of this section within the required seven days shall be released by an animal control officer to the Hall County Animal Shelter for adoption or euthanasia.
(Code 1958, § 4-3; Code 1991, § 4-1-6; Ord. No. 97-33, § VI, 6-17-1997; Ord. No. 2023-21, § IV, 8-15-2023; Ord. No. 2024-31, § III, 12-17-2024)

